      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-1022",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "jquery.json-viewer's json2html() renders any string value that matches isUrl() as a clickable `<a href=\"...\" target=\"_blank\">` link, but the generated anchor has no `rel=\"noopener\"` / `rel=\"noreferrer\"` attribute anywhere in the file. Since $.fn.jsonViewer defaults `withLinks: true` and is designed to render arbitrary/untrusted JSON (e.g. an API response) directly into the DOM via $(this).html(html), any URL-shaped string value in that JSON becomes a target=_blank link the viewing user can click, and the linked page gets an unprotected `window.opener` handle back to the host page (reverse tabnabbing / CWE-1022), letting it navigate the opener to a phishing page. This is a missing standard protection (rel=noopener/noreferrer on externally-controlled target=_blank links), not a data-flow bug -- confirmed by grepping the whole file for noopener/noreferrer/rel= and finding zero occurrences while target=\"_blank\" appears exactly once.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived independently from source and graph. json2html() (jquery.json-viewer.js) builds an anchor tag for any string value that passes isUrl(): `<a href=\"'+json+'\" class=\"json-string\" target=\"_blank\">` (line 48), gated only by `options.withLinks && isUrl(json)` (line 47). A whole-file grep confirms zero occurrences of `rel=`, `noopener`, or `noreferrer` anywhere in the file, while `target=\"_blank\"` occurs exactly once, at line 48 \u2014 so this anchor has no rel=noopener/noreferrer protection. $.fn.jsonViewer defaults `withLinks: true` (lines 120-125, within the Object.assign default options), and the resulting html string \u2014 built directly from json2html(), which recurses over arbitrary nested string/object/array JSON values supplied by the caller \u2014 is inserted as live DOM via `$(this).html(html)` at line 137, which jQuery parses and injects as real elements (not just a template string). Any URL-shaped string anywhere in the input JSON thus becomes a clickable target=_blank link lacking noopener/noreferrer, giving the linked page an unprotected window.opener handle to navigate the host page (reverse tabnabbing). Graph query confirms json2html is reachable_from_entry=true with hop_distance=0 and is itself registered as an EntryPoint (exposure=reachable, kind=handler); the specific call building the anchor at line 48 is also reachable_from_entry=true. This is a genuine missing-security-attribute defect in a library whose explicit purpose is rendering arbitrary/attacker-influenced JSON (e.g. API responses) to the DOM, not a false positive."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "json-viewer/jquery.json-viewer.js",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 47,
                  "endLine": 48
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "json2html",
                  "kind": "function"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "orion/v1": "c4abc4433334ecb7f784e7d19c8e67bbddaf939f"
          },
